senses.gloss:
सैन्धव saindhav-á, a. (í) relating to the sea 🞄(sindhu), marine, maritime;
 belonging to or 🞄coming from the Indus or Sindh;
 m. inhabitants 🞄of Sindh (pl.);
 prince of Sindh;
 horse 🞄bred in Sindh;
 m. n. rock-salt (abounding in 🞄Sindh): -ka, a. belonging to the people of 🞄Sindh;
 -khilyá, m. lump of salt (Br.);
 -śilāśakala, n. piece of rock-salt.

सैन्य sain-ya, a. belonging to or proceeding 🞄from an army (senā);
 m. soldier (pl. troops);
 🞄army (rare);
 n. army (very common);
 camp 🞄(rare): -kṣobha, m. mutiny among the 🞄troops;
 -nāyaka, m. leader of an army;
 🞄-pati, m., -pāla, m. id.;
 -maya, a. (ī) consisting 🞄of troops;
 -vāsa, m. camp of an 🞄army;
 -śiras, n. head of an army.
